# Telegram Bot API

## Do

- Default to **long polling** (`getUpdates`, `timeout > 0`, track `offset`, `allowed_updates`).
- Call `deleteWebhook` before polling if webhook was active; handle **409** clearly.
- Always call **`answerCallbackQuery`** for every `callback_query`.
- Use compact signed callback format `v1:<kind>:<action>:<id>:<nonce>`; validate server-side.
- Escape user content for HTML parse mode; chunk messages >4096 chars.
- Rate limit per chat, pairing, approvals; respect **429** `retry_after`.
- Private chats only by default; reject unauthorized chats.

## Do not

- Put secrets, full prompts, or paths in `callback_data`.
- Log bot tokens or full pairing codes.
- Process duplicate updates (broken offset handling).
- Send unredacted logs/diffs to Telegram.

## Commands

Support `/start`, `/help`, `/pair`, `/status`, `/sessions`, `/new`, `/ask`, `/approve`, `/deny`, `/logs`, `/diff`, `/stop`, `/workspace`, `/mcp`, `/hooks`, `/events`, `/loopback`, `/settings`.
